<title>FRANCE: Metaleurop 95/96 net profit 42 mln Ffr.</title>
<headline>Metaleurop 95/96 net profit 42 mln Ffr.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to Sept 30, 1996.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of French francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net attributable profit		     42  vs  loss     122</p>
<p>    Operating profit				23  vs  loss     165</p>
<p>    Pre-tax, pre-exceptional loss	     29  vs  loss     263</p>
<p>    Exceptional gains			     78  vs	     151</p>
<p>    Net financial loss			    52  vs  loss	98</p>
<p>    Turnover				     4,293  up four percent</p>
<p>NOTE - Metaleurop gave its results in a statement. It said the improvement in operating profit was due to cost cutting and restructuring programmes, suppported by positive development in lead, germanium and indium markets. However, zinc prices remained insufficient, it said. The turnround in operating results also reflected substantial productivity gains and a 10 percent reduction in the group workforce.</p>
<p>Capital expenditure for the 1995/96 year totalled 282 million francs and was mainly devoted to the new Nordenham lead smelter, construction of a smelting reactor in the zinc recycling plant at Harzer Zink and restructuring programmes.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452 pnt</p>
